        "items": [
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Biotechnology vs pharmacy careers differ mainly in licensing and daily work: pharmacy leads to dispensing, drug regulation, manufacturing and quality roles with a clear registration route, while biotechnology leads to research, bioprocess and product roles with less defined entry."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Choose pharmacy for a regulated, structured path with community or industry roles, and biotechnology for research and product development that may need further study."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Check official bodies and avoid agents promising guaranteed jobs."
          }
        ]
      },
      "type": "proof",
      "title": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test"
